From f7ade5520dee7a2673eac9ad6cdedeb4f8b94ede Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Calogero Mandracchia <calogero@efebia.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:34:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] channels: keep idle-started channel input until it is
 recorded

Idle delivery tagged nothing and dropped a batch as soon as the thread
accepted a new turn, so an interrupt before recording lost it. Both paths
now tag the user message with the batch id and keep the batch until the
core confirms it was recorded. An aborted turn returns its batch to the
head of the queue; a turn cancelled before it started returns it when the
next regular turn starts; a completed turn that did not record it still
discards it, so a blocking input hook cannot cause a retry loop.
